    "question": "Tyson can swim at a speed of 3 miles per hour in a lake and 2.5 mph in an ocean. This season, half his races happened in lakes and half his races happened in the ocean. He had ten total races, each of which was 3 miles long. How much time did he spend in his races?",
    "gold": "11",
    "answer": "He did 5 races in the lake because 10 / 2 = <<10/2=5>>5\nHe did 5 races in the ocean because 10 / 2 = <<10/2=5>>5\nHe raced 15 miles in the lake because 5 x 3 = <<5*3=15>>15\nHis lake races took 6 hours because 15 / 2.5 = <<15/2.5=6>>6\nHe raced 15 miles in the ocean because 5 x 3 = <<5*3=15>>15\nHis ocean races took 5 hours because 15 / 3 = <<15/3=5>>5\nHe spent 11 hours racing because 5 + 6 = <<5+6=11>>11\n#### 11"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total time Tyson spent in his races, we need to calculate the time spent in the lake races and the time spent in the ocean races separately, and then sum these times.\n\nFirst, let's find out how many races Tyson had in each type of water. Since he had ten total races and half of them were in lakes and half were in the ocean, we have:\n\\[ \\text{Number of lake races} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Number of ocean races} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the time spent in the lake races. Tyson swims in the lake at a speed of 3 miles per hour. Each race is 3 miles long. Therefore, the time spent in each lake race is:\n\\[ \\text{Time per lake race} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 1 \\text{ hour} \\]\nSince he had 5 lake races, the total time spent in the lake races is:\n\\[ \\text{Total time in lake races} = 5 \\times 1 \\text{ hour} = 5 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the time spent in the ocean races. Tyson swims in the ocean at a speed of 2.5 miles per hour. Each race is 3 miles long. Therefore, the time spent in each ocean race is:\n\\[ \\text{Time per ocean race} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{2.5 \\text{ miles per hour}} = \\frac{3}{2.5} = 1.2 \\text{ hours} \\]\nSince he had 5 ocean races, the total time spent in the ocean races is:\n\\[ \\text{Total time in ocean races} = 5 \\times 1.2 \\text{ hours} = 6 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nFinally, we sum the time spent in the lake races and the time spent in the ocean races to get the total time spent in all races:\n\\[ \\text{Total time} = 5 \\text{ hours} + 6 \\text{ hours} = 11 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nThus, the total time Tyson spent in his races is:\n\\[ \\boxed{11} \\]",
